  "review": {
    "verdict": "PASS",
    "feedback": "Reviewed the four fixed statements against the imported ThirtyCofactorCubePrimeExtraction signatures. cofactor_M_cases correctly requires n >= 1; without it n = 0 gives product 18, so the hypothesis is essential. L_lower_bound correctly requires M > 0, n >= 2 and 3n < r, and proves 9M + 1 <= L. L_upper_bound correctly requires M > 0, n >= 104 and 3r < 10n, and proves 927L < 10400M. Q_dvd_sq_pair_covering assumes n >= 104, the two strict interval bounds, and L*Q = r^2; Q > 0 follows from n >= 104, so this is the intended Q | r^2 setting. The four displayed ranges are exactly the integer consequences of the two bounds for M in {1,2,3,6}. The imported cofactor_M_mul_sq matches the hL hypothesis and is applied correctly. No name overstates: the last theorem is only a covering statement for (M,L), not existence of all pairs, Pell completeness, Q not dividing r^2, or exclusion of the branch. No mathematical scope or positivity issue found."
  },
